    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0093" n="61" xml:id="pg61"/>

                <head>37. Telegram From the Embassy in Cuba to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d37-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-03-16T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                                1958—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>543. Guell informed us night March 15: <list>
                        <label>(A)</label>
                        <item>GOC greatly concerned over steps taken Deptel 492.<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d37-f2"/></item>
                        <label>(B)</label>
                        <item>If GOC had been forewarned that MAP equipment was to be held back,
                            they would have purchased such equipment from other countries.</item>
                        <label>(C)</label>
                        <item>Present GOC equipment is obsolete and worn. As GOC is increasing size
                            of army, it is especially anxious to receive rifles (Deptel 492).</item>
                        <label>(D)</label>
                        <item>Guell will as soon as possible prepare note from GOC to US for
                            presentation.</item>
                        <label>(E)</label>
                        <item>It will be impossible to avoid publicity regarding steps taken Deptel
                            492.</item>
                        <label>(F)</label>
                        <item>Reaffirmed that elections will be postponed and when held will be
                            completely honest (Embtel 536<anchor n="3" xml:id="d37-f3"/>).</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>I conveyed assurances that there was no change in friendly attitude of US to GOC
                    and again pointed out embarrassing position of US due to overwhelming criticism
                    from Congress and press.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
